<title>UZBEKISTAN: Uzbekistan to fight to stay big cotton exporter.</title>
<headline>Uzbekistan to fight to stay big cotton exporter.</headline>
<dateline>TASHKENT 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uzbekistan will fight hard to maintain its place as the world's second largest cotton exporter, Uzbek President Islam Karimov said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe our main task is to secure and strengthen Uzbekistan's cotton trade,&quot; he said in an address to the International Cotton Advisory Committee (ICAC).</p>
<p>Sources at the agriculture ministry said Uzbekistan planned to harvest around four million tonnes of raw cotton in 1996. It harvested 3.9 million tonnes of raw cotton in 1995, according to official figures.</p>
<p>Main buyers are Switzerland, Britain, Holland, South Korea, Turkey and Austria.</p>
